<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Offset On Curved Surfaces</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> When you capture with a ball probe on a curved surface (like sphere, cylinder, circular hole, round slot) it is important to determine from which side you got the points. This is because the localiser returns co-ordinates of the centre of its probe. In order to calculate the correct radius KUBE needs to know in what direction the offset must be made. In case of ball probes the offset is equal to the probe radius.</p>
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">In case when you</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>captured from outside</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">, the radius will be decreased to match the real radius of the object.</span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">In case when you</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>captured from inside</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">, the radius will be increased to match the real radius of the object.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
